# constraint_union_full_type.tkr — the SM-G12 (crumb 0018) constraint-term-broadening anchor.
# `<T: []A | A | error>` (the CI-965 form) now parses: a constraint term is a full type, not just a
# bare name. `case::entry()` instantiates the constrained generic with T = A, exercising the new
# `ConstraintType` disjunct alongside the pre-existing `ConstraintAtom` alternatives.

Feature: constraint_union_full_type — a disjunctive constraint term accepts a slice/named/error mix

